2186501030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501202 #edb/ref 1069 "q-91347" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501202 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501202 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{3}=-343.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501202 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4309379-1166-58a1-b1ee-b77ecf90fd3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501202 #edb/ref 1074 "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =-343 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-343} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{(-7)^{3}} \\\\ x & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{3}=-512.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb6a3551-b7c8-5448-9dd7-361a94a204ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501224 #edb/ref 1074 "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =-512 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-512} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{(-8)^{3}} \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the real solution to the equation $(x-5)^{3}=-27.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e173cb82-cae9-5da1-9ec4-a1b561689a6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501229 #edb/ref 1074 "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$\nSince $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{3} & =-27 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(x-5)^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\ x-5 & =\\sqrt[3]{(-3)^{3}} \\\\ x-5 & =-3 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111455" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the real solution to the equation $3(x+7)^{9}=1\\,536.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea193efd-d8e8-59fc-adc1-1d1595da20e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501233 #edb/ref 1074 "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x+7)^{9}$ term and then taking the $9$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x+7)^{9}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+7)^{9} & =1\\,536 \\\\ (x+7)^{9} & =512\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $9$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=9$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+7)^{9} & =512 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{(x+7)^{9}} & =\\sqrt[9]{512} \\\\ x+7 & =\\sqrt[9]{{2}^{9}} \\\\ x+7 & =2 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
